CONTEXT.md:324:- A **Stage Push** uses the current **Task Branch** upstream when one exists.
CONTEXT.md:325:- A **Stage Push** creates an upstream on `origin` when the current **Task Branch** has no upstream.
CONTEXT.md:326:- A **Stage Push** happens before any auto-merge attempt.
CONTEXT.md:327:- **Task Branch Integration** must not force-push a **Task Branch** after **Stage Push**.
CONTEXT.md:328:- Symphony does not push the **Loop-Start Branch** after auto-merge.
CONTEXT.md:333:- Runtime Settings configure **Stage Goal Handoff** with `goal.enabled` on a stage.
CONTEXT.md:335:- Bootstrapped Runtime Settings include `goal.enabled` as `false` in each example stage.
CONTEXT.md:353:- **Goal Usage** remains in **Runtime State** when a task moves from running to retrying or attention-needed state.
CONTEXT.md:356:- **Stage Goal Handoff** does not change retry, completion, status transition, commit, push, auto-merge, or Batch Pull Request behavior.
CONTEXT.md:382:- Ordered Queue completion may trigger existing **Batch Pull Request** behavior for completed queued work.
CONTEXT.md:386:- A **Batch Pull Request** represents the combined task work already integrated into the **Loop-Start Branch**.
CONTEXT.md:387:- Symphony may open a **Batch Pull Request** after reaching **Orchestration Idle**.
CONTEXT.md:388:- Symphony must not open a **Batch Pull Request** while any issue remains in a **Merge Attention Status**.
CONTEXT.md:389:- Symphony must not open a **Batch Pull Request** while any issue has unresolved orchestration attention.
CONTEXT.md:390:- A **Batch Pull Request** uses the **Loop-Start Branch** as its head branch.
CONTEXT.md:391:- A **Batch Pull Request** uses the configured **Pull Request Base Branch** as its base branch.
CONTEXT.md:392:- Symphony may retry opening a **Batch Pull Request** after a failed attempt when **Orchestration Idle** is reached again.
CONTEXT.md:393:- Symphony must not create a duplicate **Batch Pull Request** for the same head and base branches.
CONTEXT.md:394:- A **Pull Request Base Branch** must be configured explicitly in Runtime Settings.
CONTEXT.md:395:- The **Runtime Settings** may contain a **Pull Request Policy**.
CONTEXT.md:396:- The **Pull Request Policy** controls whether Symphony opens a **Batch Pull Request** after **Orchestration Idle**.
CONTEXT.md:397:- The default **Pull Request Policy** disables automatic **Batch Pull Request** creation.
CONTEXT.md:398:- A **Pull Request Base Branch** is required when the **Pull Request Policy** enables automatic **Batch Pull Request** creation.
CONTEXT.md:399:- The **Pull Request Policy** may define **Pull Request Templates** for the **Batch Pull Request** title and body.
CONTEXT.md:401:- A **Batch Branch Push** happens before opening a **Batch Pull Request**.
CONTEXT.md:403:- A failed **Batch Branch Push** prevents the **Batch Pull Request** from being opened.
CONTEXT.md:405:- Runtime State records Batch Pull Request handoff attempts, completions, and retryable failures.
CONTEXT.md:417:- The **Web Dashboard** should show issue metadata by default and expose task execution details only when they help the operator understand running, retrying, or attention-needed work.
CONTEXT.md:419:- The **Web Dashboard** should present Readiness Gaps and the Runtime State global last error as attention banners.
CONTEXT.md:427:- **Audio Notification Configuration** does not change **Runtime Settings**.
CONTEXT.md:432:- A **Web Dashboard** may emit an **Audio Notification** after observing a Runtime State transition that needs user attention.
CONTEXT.md:482:> **Domain expert:** "No, a **Stage Push** only follows a successful **Stage Commit**."
CONTEXT.md:484:> **Domain expert:** "No, it pushes the currently checked-out **Task Branch**, because the agent may be running inside an **Agent Worktree**."
CONTEXT.md:485:> **Dev:** "What if the current **Task Branch** has no upstream yet?"
CONTEXT.md:487:> **Dev:** "If the **Stage Commit** succeeds but the **Stage Push** fails, should Symphony still move the issue to the success state?"
CONTEXT.md:496:> **Domain expert:** "No, the **Web Dashboard** emits **Audio Notifications** only for observed Runtime State transitions that need user attention."
CONTEXT.md:505:> **Dev:** "Should completion and attention use the same sound file?"
CONTEXT.md:509:> **Dev:** "If work finishes and a task needs attention at the same time, should both tones play?"
CONTEXT.md:519:- "push the code in every step" was used to mean pushing after each successful stage-level commit; resolved: use **Stage Push** for the optional push that follows a **Stage Commit**.
CONTEXT.md:520:- "push to the branch that we are in" was used to mean pushing the currently checked-out **Task Branch**, especially from an **Agent Worktree**.
CONTEXT.md:527:- "Open PR after finishing all the tasks" was used to mean opening one pull request for combined task work; resolved: use **Batch Pull Request**, opened from the **Loop-Start Branch** after **Orchestration Idle**.
CONTEXT.md:528:- "base branch" for automatic PR creation was ambiguous because the **Loop-Start Branch** is the head of the **Batch Pull Request**; resolved: use configured **Pull Request Base Branch** for the target branch.
CONTEXT.md:529:- "merge the worktrees" was used to mean integrating completed **Task Branches**; resolved: Symphony fast-forward merges **Task Branches** into the **Loop-Start Branch**, not Agent Worktrees.
CONTEXT.md:530:- ".symphonyignore" was used to mean a repository-owned rule for files agents must not modify; resolved: use **Protected Path Policy** stored in **Runtime Settings** for the first version.
CONTEXT.md:532:- "commit stage tags" was used to mean metadata that chooses a Stage Commit type or tag; resolved: use **Stage Commit Classification**.
docs/adr/0006-browser-local-audio-notifications.md:9:The Web Dashboard receives Runtime State snapshots through the Live Dashboard Connection. Operators need an opt-in browser sound when Symphony needs attention or active work finishes, but audio preferences are local browser behavior and should not change the Runtime Contract.
docs/adr/0006-browser-local-audio-notifications.md:15:The initial Runtime State snapshot never emits an Audio Notification. A Work Became Idle transition emits the completion tone when running and retrying counts both reach zero after previously having running or retrying work. A Task Needs Attention transition emits the attention tone when a new Runtime State issue error appears.
docs/adr/0006-browser-local-audio-notifications.md:21:Audio Notifications remain browser-local and opt-in. Symphony does not add backend notification events, Runtime Settings, audio assets, or notification history for this behavior.
docs/adr/0008-github-rate-limit-pause.md:17:This pause applies to candidate issue polling. It does not change Runtime Settings defaults, Stage Commit, Stage Push, Task Branch cleanup, auto-merge, or per-task retry semantics.
